<Base title="Paid partnerships & gifting" description="How Amyzing Finds handles paid partnerships, gifted visits and editorial independence.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <span class="eyebrow">Small print</span>
      <h1>Paid partnerships &amp; gifting</h1>
      <p class="lede">The short version: if someone paid, or gave me something for free, I say so. Every time, at the top.</p>
      <h2>Paid partnerships</h2>
      <p>Where a business has paid for a post, a visit or a series, the Instagram post is marked as a paid partnership and the article on this site carries a “Paid partnership” label at the top. This follows the UK Advertising Standards Authority (ASA) and Competition and Markets Authority (CMA) guidance on influencer marketing.</p>
      <h2>Gifted visits</h2>
      <p>Sometimes a meal, a stay or a ticket is provided for free in exchange for consideration of a feature. Those are labelled “Gifted”. A gift buys a visit, not a verdict.</p>
      <h2>What doesn’t change</h2>
      <p>Nobody approves my wording. I only feature places I’d send a friend to. If I don’t like somewhere, I don’t write about it, paid or not.</p>
      <h2>Ads on this site</h2>
      <p>This site doesn’t currently run display advertising. If that changes, this page will say so.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
